<Folder><name>Main path: Sindorim → Dorimcheon → Anyangcheon embankment (3.3 km)</name>
<Placemark><name>Sindorim Stn → Dorimcheon Stn → Anyangcheon embankment (Sinjeong Bridge → Gocheok Bridge), 3.3 km</name><description><![CDATA[3.3 km<br>1. Dorimcheon stream path and Anyangcheon east-bank path (OSM cycleway geometry)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-0</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>126.891267,37.509589,0 126.891611,37.509523,0 126.891305,37.510014,0 126.891077,37.510385,0 126.890858,37.510658,0 126.890731,37.510762,0 126.890673,37.510810,0 126.889816,37.511407,0 126.889205,37.511873,0 126.888788,37.512130,0 126.888440,37.512312,0 126.887777,37.512600,0 126.886951,37.512910,0 126.886208,37.513285,0 126.885961,37.513391,0 126.884955,37.513685,0 126.883748,37.514259,0 126.883382,37.514454,0 126.882970,37.514719,0 126.882744,37.514852,0 126.882456,37.514977,0 126.882232,37.515152,0 126.881536,37.515587,0 126.881430,37.515609,0 126.881342,37.515629,0 126.881249,37.515635,0 126.881151,37.515634,0 126.881054,37.515623,0 126.881054,37.515623,0 126.880987,37.515609,0 126.880947,37.515590,0 126.880886,37.515544,0 126.880856,37.515493,0 126.880821,37.515389,0 126.880794,37.515269,0 126.880761,37.515210,0 126.879943,37.514279,0 126.879887,37.514229,0 126.879834,37.514192,0 126.879782,37.514167,0 126.879712,37.514157,0 126.879575,37.514166,0 126.879529,37.514164,0 126.879479,37.514143,0 126.879414,37.514086,0 126.879414,37.514086,0 126.879244,37.513890,0 126.879244,37.513890,0 126.879089,37.513728,0 126.879049,37.513664,0 126.879036,37.513599,0 126.879031,37.513453,0 126.879021,37.513345,0 126.878975,37.513263,0 126.878874,37.513143,0 126.878191,37.512410,0 126.874806,37.508497,0 126.874719,37.508366,0 126.874457,37.507808,0 126.874308,37.507592,0 126.874247,37.507504,0 126.874201,37.507423,0 126.874122,37.507092,0 126.873792,37.506517,0 126.873780,37.506481,0 126.873737,37.506348,0 126.873452,37.505474,0 126.873402,37.505331,0 126.873252,37.504901,0 126.872680,37.503238,0 126.871688,37.500352,0 126.871638,37.500206,0 126.871638,37.500206,0 126.871394,37.499491,0 126.871246,37.499116,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>1. Start – Sindorim Station exit 6</name><description><![CDATA[Lines 1 and 2. From exit 6 walk 30 m to the Dorimcheon stream and turn left (north-west) onto the streamside path. Cherry trees line both banks.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/36733988?lng=126.8912670&lat=37.5095890&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.891267,37.509589,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Dorimcheon Station</name><description><![CDATA[Line 2 branch. The stream path passes right below the station; keep following the water towards the Anyangcheon.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13479394?lng=126.8826420&lat=37.5144740&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.882642,37.514474,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Sinjeong Bridge – join the Anyangcheon embankment</name><description><![CDATA[Where the Dorimcheon meets the Anyangcheon. Turn left (south) and follow the embankment path on the Guro side; this is the cherry-blossom tunnel section.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/18955382?lng=126.8799100&lat=37.5166830&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.879910,37.516683,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. End – Gocheok Bridge</name><description><![CDATA[End of the embankment cherry road. Gocheok Sky Dome is just across the bridge; Guil Station (line 1) is 800 m east.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/18956792?lng=126.8703250&lat=37.4992040&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.870325,37.499204,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Yeouido Yunjung-ro (2.6 km)</name>
<Placemark><name>National Assembly Stn → Yunjung-ro (Yeouiseo-ro) cherry road → Mapo Bridge south end, 2.6 km</name><description><![CDATA[2.6 km<br>1. Station to Yeouiseo-ro (router) (approx.)<br>2. Yeouiseo-ro / Yunjung-ro (OSM road geometry; walk the riverside pavement)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-1</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>126.916160,37.528733,0 126.915965,37.528613,0 126.915047,37.528048,0 126.914538,37.527719,0 126.914503,37.527696,0 126.914041,37.528165,0 126.912682,37.529566,0 126.912615,37.529532,0 126.912518,37.529504,0 126.912455,37.529487,0 126.912479,37.529427,0 126.912455,37.529487,0 126.911609,37.531702,0 126.911561,37.531817,0 126.911436,37.532115,0 126.911393,37.532282,0 126.911363,37.532459,0 126.911362,37.532598,0 126.911385,37.532745,0 126.911407,37.532861,0 126.911472,37.532999,0 126.911550,37.533125,0 126.911618,37.533243,0 126.911908,37.533506,0 126.911998,37.533564,0 126.912109,37.533623,0 126.912230,37.533667,0 126.912350,37.533698,0 126.912458,37.533716,0 126.912579,37.533725,0 126.912838,37.533718,0 126.914248,37.533613,0 126.914458,37.533597,0 126.915892,37.533465,0 126.917020,37.533315,0 126.917922,37.533064,0 126.918141,37.533002,0 126.918224,37.532975,0 126.918224,37.532975,0 126.920192,37.532367,0 126.920192,37.532367,0 126.920219,37.532358,0 126.920219,37.532358,0 126.920270,37.532342,0 126.920906,37.532153,0 126.921160,37.532082,0 126.921410,37.532025,0 126.921660,37.531968,0 126.921660,37.531968,0 126.922133,37.531828,0 126.922267,37.531787,0 126.923704,37.531363,0 126.924435,37.531126,0 126.924570,37.531085,0 126.925087,37.530922,0 126.925528,37.530785,0 126.925528,37.530785,0 126.925931,37.530655,0 126.926515,37.530449,0 126.927305,37.530167,0 126.927305,37.530167,0 126.927958,37.529857,0 126.928095,37.529792,0 126.928095,37.529792,0 126.928341,37.529672,0 126.929027,37.529336,0 126.929234,37.529229,0 126.929234,37.529229,0 126.929489,37.529093,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>1. Start – National Assembly Station exit 6</name><description><![CDATA[Line 9. Walk around the back of the National Assembly to Yeouiseo-ro, the road along the Han River.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/21406277?lng=126.9161650&lat=37.5287280&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.916165,37.528728,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Yunjung-ro cherry road</name><description><![CDATA[Seoul's best-known cherry avenue: about 1,800 trees along the river. During the festival (early–mid April) the road is closed to cars and very crowded; go early morning or after dark when it is lit.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13491740?lng=126.9198600&lat=37.5324850&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.919860,37.532485,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. End – Mapo Bridge south end (Han River Park)</name><description><![CDATA[Yunjung-ro ends near Mapo Bridge. Continue into Yeouido Han River Park for picnic lawns, or walk 15 min to Yeouinaru Station (line 5).<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/31786878?lng=126.9310020&lat=37.5290260&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.931002,37.529026,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Seokchon Lake loop (3.4 km)</name>
<Placemark><name>Jamsil Stn → around Seokchon Lake (West and East lakes) → Jamsil Stn, 3.4 km</name><description><![CDATA[3.4 km<br>1. Lakeside loop (pedestrian router; follow the lakeside promenade where the line uses the road) (approx.)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-2</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>127.100211,37.513348,0 127.100362,37.513182,0 127.100450,37.513074,0 127.100751,37.512721,0 127.101105,37.512250,0 127.101302,37.512005,0 127.101830,37.511372,0 127.101578,37.511233,0 127.101446,37.511167,0 127.101424,37.511157,0 127.101379,37.511162,0 127.101375,37.511142,0 127.101314,37.511071,0 127.100606,37.510733,0 127.100438,37.510653,0 127.099950,37.510456,0 127.099496,37.510325,0 127.099433,37.510307,0 127.099433,37.510307,0 127.099065,37.510202,0 127.098320,37.510102,0 127.098093,37.510109,0 127.097781,37.510118,0 127.097758,37.510021,0 127.097735,37.509915,0 127.097724,37.509869,0 127.097625,37.509763,0 127.097607,37.509065,0 127.097594,37.508848,0 127.097563,37.508257,0 127.097509,37.507640,0 127.097518,37.507416,0 127.097520,37.507357,0 127.097537,37.506650,0 127.097628,37.506600,0 127.098283,37.506517,0 127.098283,37.506517,0 127.098299,37.506515,0 127.098815,37.506541,0 127.099144,37.506572,0 127.099228,37.506497,0 127.099641,37.506586,0 127.100700,37.506974,0 127.100729,37.506917,0 127.101398,37.507150,0 127.101670,37.507279,0 127.102010,37.507441,0 127.102179,37.507536,0 127.102179,37.507536,0 127.102840,37.507906,0 127.103687,37.508381,0 127.103834,37.508396,0 127.103990,37.508393,0 127.104097,37.508448,0 127.104292,37.508558,0 127.104350,37.508591,0 127.104363,37.508598,0 127.104776,37.508217,0 127.105037,37.507962,0 127.105298,37.507706,0 127.105513,37.507823,0 127.106552,37.508589,0 127.106552,37.508589,0 127.106259,37.508857,0 127.105958,37.509137,0 127.105669,37.509398,0 127.105377,37.509675,0 127.106219,37.510344,0 127.106129,37.510403,0 127.106150,37.510420,0 127.106075,37.510476,0 127.106067,37.510482,0 127.105922,37.510591,0 127.106616,37.511163,0 127.106888,37.511456,0 127.106888,37.511456,0 127.106616,37.511163,0 127.105922,37.510591,0 127.105428,37.510230,0 127.105234,37.510102,0 127.105132,37.510042,0 127.105087,37.510015,0 127.104999,37.509964,0 127.104826,37.509863,0 127.104531,37.509680,0 127.104401,37.509609,0 127.104323,37.509569,0 127.104084,37.509524,0 127.103957,37.509538,0 127.103748,37.509638,0 127.103558,37.509866,0 127.103401,37.509747,0 127.103329,37.509830,0 127.103025,37.510159,0 127.102955,37.510239,0 127.102205,37.511093,0 127.102235,37.511197,0 127.102173,37.511279,0 127.102111,37.511343,0 127.102000,37.511472,0 127.102000,37.511472,0 127.101830,37.511372,0 127.101302,37.512005,0 127.101105,37.512250,0 127.100751,37.512721,0 127.100450,37.513074,0 127.100362,37.513182,0 127.100211,37.513348,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>1. Start / End – Jamsil Station (line 2)</name><description><![CDATA[Exit 2 or 3 for the lake. The loop around both lakes is about 2.5 km on the promenade; this line adds the walk from the station.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13307432?lng=127.1001870&lat=37.5133490&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>127.100187,37.513349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Seokchon Lake – West Lake</name><description><![CDATA[Cherry trees ring the whole lake; the west lake is quieter. Lotte World's Magic Island sits in the east lake.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/18849462?lng=127.0995690&lat=37.5076910&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>127.099569,37.507691,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Seokchon Lake – East Lake</name><description><![CDATA[Busiest stretch during the Seokchon Lake Cherry Blossom Festival (early April), with Lotte World Tower behind the blossoms.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/21251977?lng=127.1052550&lat=37.5112630&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>127.105255,37.511263,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
