<Placemark><name>1. Start – National Theatre of Korea</name><description><![CDATA[Bus 01A/01B from Dongguk University Station (line 3). The loop road starts behind the theatre; cars are banned, so walk in the middle.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/11621552?lng=126.9996170&lat=37.5526710&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.999617,37.552671,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. North Loop cherry section</name><description><![CDATA[Gentle, shaded 3 km road with cherry trees overhead and views of the city below. Benches and a café at the midway rest area.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1478186923?lng=126.9881210&lat=37.5551680&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.988121,37.555168,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. End – Namsan Library</name><description><![CDATA[The loop road ends by the library and Baekbeom Square. Myeongdong Station (line 4) is 15 min downhill.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/11592008?lng=126.9813370&lat=37.5530600&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.981337,37.553060,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
